{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevJb44q2FEDdqmiUqvHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions in this repository:**\n- Controllers use `@RestController` with `@PostMapping` for actions\n- State-changing operations return the modified resource via `ResponseEntity`\n- Error handling: `ConflictException` for 409, `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404\n- Every 409 conflict needs an `ErrorCode` from the enum\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with `jsonPath` assertions for response verification\n- Error responses wrapped in `ApiError` structure with code/message fields\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` – Add `@PostMapping` method for confirm operation (unavoidable)\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` – Add test cases for confirm scenarios (required for acceptance)\n3. `ApiError.kt` – Add new `ErrorCode` for invalid state transition (necessary for 409 response with proper error code)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if endpoint registration conflicts\n- Idempotent behavior (confirming CONFIRMED succeeds) must not be handled as error\n- Adding `ErrorCode` affects a shared error definition file\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None – all cases are clearly defined in the ticket.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This code will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment (409 conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method `confirm()` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Takes the shipment ID from the path\n   - Fetches the shipment (throw 404 if not found)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code (409)\n   - If status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment (with 200 OK status)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and changes status to CONFIRMED`\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment without changing it (idempotent)`\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409 and proper error code`\n   - `reports an unknown shipment through the error envelope (404)`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate `ShipmentService` layer: Rejected because the existing codebase has logic directly in controllers, and adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring beyond this ticket's scope.\n- Using an existing ErrorCode (e.g., VALIDATION_FAILED): Rejected because VALIDATION_FAILED is for bad input validation, not state transitions. A new domain-specific code (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) is more consistent with existing patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Scenario | Read | Write | Response | Status |\n|----------|------|-------|----------|--------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | Shipment by ID | Updated shipment to store | Shipment object | 200 OK |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | Shipment by ID | None | Shipment object | 200 OK |\n| CANCELLED → error | Shipment by ID | None | Error envelope | 409 Conflict |\n| Unknown ID | Not found | None | Error envelope | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **Test 1** (happy path): Create shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2** (idempotent): Confirm twice, verify second succeeds and status unchanged\n- **Test 3** (cancelled): Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n- **Test 4** (not found): Confirm non-existent ID, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_read_input_tokens":17515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1236},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a57b38d-b17b-4389-baa2-da666b5d5840","uuid":"64a655a2-a29d-4b12-9f49-edf6bda6f64b","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:23:21.698Z","request_id":"req_011CevJb3QtDN11i2Hd8EeVD"}
